{"conditionalSetIds":[],"forecasterId":"demographics-ai-2036:run2:labor:bayes","informationSetArtifactId":"sha256:78b9678b555bcab4b41f977809d8fbcd46a8b7be9773965a71697b491336a5ed","modelForecastIds":[],"modelUse":"none","prediction":{"kind":"binary","positiveOutcomeId":"yes","probability":0.18},"questionHash":"sha256:cfe468fa9439bedeee3804a35583667745f13831322e2c91a89c02a1b211413b","questionId":"demographics-ai-2036-cq5","questionVersion":"1.0.0","rationale":"PRIOR: Historian's 22, from marginal A=0.35 and P(B|A)=0.62.\n\nCONJUNCT A (ICE BofA MOVE averages >=105 over Jan 2027 - Dec 2036). Prior 0.35 (Historian: ~6-8 of ~28 rolling 10-yr windows clear it; full-history mean 93.6 since 1988 with the start date contested — \"ICE's own data page says history from 1996\"; 10-year average ~75 per Carmignac; 2017-19 ~55; 2022 cycle ~130; so 105 is MATERIALLY ABOVE the full-history mean). EVIDENCE 1, Scout's level telemetry: 70.9 as of Jul 17 2026 (tracker page); 65.7-66bp on a Convex page where \"it gives no date for that reading\" and \"it may be stale\"; 103.01 \"by mid-2026\" (Pulse, time-dependent and undated); 115 on an NBot summary \"last updated April 8, 2026\"; a seven-day decline to 66.87, \"its lowest level since 2021\", \"probably from October 2025\" but carrying no date. Scout's own verdict: \"These cannot be reconciled; I could not find a confirmed October 2026 close and treat the level as UNVERIFIED AT MY HORIZON\". LR UNJUSTIFIABLE AT ANY RATIO — a signal spanning 66 to 115 with contested or absent dates cannot move a posterior in either direction. SET TO 1.0 AND FLAGGED. This is the single worst-instrumented input in the question set and the main place where this seat's failure mode (weak evidence asserted confidently) would bite.\n\nEVIDENCE 2, Fermi's level-scaling constraint, which IS usable because it is a ratio rather than a level reading: MOVE is 1-month implied Treasury yield vol in annualized bp, scaling roughly as k x (nominal yield level) x (policy